# WPF & MVVM Rules

- Use `CommunityToolkit.Mvvm` for ViewModels:
  - Inherit from `ObservableObject`.
  - Use `[ObservableProperty]` and `[RelayCommand]` attributes.
- Keep View code-behind (`.xaml.cs`) minimal: only pure UI interactions like mouse drag or focus.
- Never write business logic or database access inside code-behind.
- Group styles and brushes into resource dictionaries in `Presentation/Themes/`.
- Provide `AutomationProperties.Name` on buttons and interactive components for screen readers.
- Keep layout responsive and DPI-aware; use device-independent units.
